  "text": "Count every cell in your body and fewer than half of them are yours. Around thirty trillion human cells. Around thirty eight trillion bacteria. Most of them live in your gut, packed tighter than any city on Earth. They are not passengers. They break down fibre your own enzymes cannot touch. They manufacture vitamins you do not make yourself, and hand them straight over. And early on, they teach your immune system what is safe to leave alone. There are real links between that crowd and your mood, along the nerve joining gut to brain. How much of that is cause and how much is coincidence is still being argued over. The startling one is already clinical. Transplanting a healthy person's gut bacteria cures infections antibiotics cannot. You are not one organism. You are a very well managed crowd. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
